Use configureMCMC() with the additional argument useConjugacy = FALSE.  Very strong chances the conjugacy checking is getting into a giant recursive mess with your model structure.

This will make it so the resulting MCMC won't use conjugate (Gibbs) sampling for any dimensions; but if you know parts of your model that are conjugate, you always have the option to manually add conjugate samplers to the MCMC configuration object later.

Let me know if this works.

