For interested list-readers: I set up a GitHub branch with one approach to provide more flexible cross-validation.

It is on a GitHub branch called "flexible-crossValidation".  To install from this branch, one can do:

library(devtools)
install_github("nimble-dev/nimble", ref = "flexible-crossValidation", subdir = "packages/nimble")

The way we trigger continuous-integration testing is by making a pull-request on a branch, so I have done so for that purpose.  The PR describes the code changes: https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/pull/833

Henry, let me know how this works for you.  It is just a hasty first try.  We can iterate off-list if we need to get into details.

Perry

